
What is polymorphism ?
=> Polymorphism is concept by which can we can perform a single task in different way.      OR
   - That single entity behaves differently in different cases.

   e.g. - Liquid - 1. Water changes to solid when it frozen. / water changes to gas when it is heated.

Note - Polymorphism only supports in methods.

Types of Polymorphism :
    1. Static Polymorphism
    2. Dynamic Polymorphism


1. Static Polymorphism :
    - A polymorphism exabit during compilation.
    - binding is performed at compile-time, it also known as early binding.


2. Dynamic Polymorphism :
    - A polymorphism exabit during runtime.
    


